#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd5464c3-57fd-5a2c-9a84-afac2b14f2eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291751} {:answer/id #uuid "57237e18-6867-5e6f-8422-9eef93243cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291752} {:answer/id #uuid "42bcef1a-8023-5194-b0a5-69fadb2e4808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291753} {:answer/id #uuid "63dc607c-cf41-51a5-a94e-62efbc2b157c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291754} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0bd01f-3396-5cfa-9752-a13677eaaff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63dc607c-cf41-51a5-a94e-62efbc2b157c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291754} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f049f9b-3f8f-53af-801a-1c9505f14d7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f36e193-cfb7-556d-862d-7ca0f147ebca" :question/math-academy-id "q-102799" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y=-x \\\\ 2y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=0 \\\\ 2y=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c963c1-98e9-5a2d-a5c7-0f6d04dbda30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291758} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c36bc2-4930-5d0c-9a5f-14d8dcb8f959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291759} {:answer/id #uuid "590404f5-f3f8-532b-aeb2-8ac76e440df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291760} {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} {:answer/id #uuid "850318a6-1a4d-5307-b80c-b8e0f486b5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca356f0b-e266-5dae-b876-0c22bbf0bfe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95af1977-8d23-5d4e-89a9-245a921e273b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102806" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5=2x-3y \\\\ 4x=y-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a7d0dd9-ef90-5a78-b26d-87a0a2ad4883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291765} {:answer/id #uuid "427c887c-8dd5-543f-ad02-0b332476891a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291766} {:answer/id #uuid "3baaea1d-e683-5f80-bdf0-a1b149859a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291767} {:answer/id #uuid "1e429afb-5070-5548-afe7-b4fbfcfcb1dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291768} {:answer/id #uuid "31f1a90f-04d1-58c6-a0e6-80f1b1a7c7d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e429afb-5070-5548-afe7-b4fbfcfcb1dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291768} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a047a2-2e31-5d1c-8287-e4210414ae62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4330c109-1f4a-587b-b6ac-d3c48b67916a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32033" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=0 \\\\ -3x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a27f9476-02bb-5947-a1d3-d4be7c516d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291772} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c1bb03-9d37-5f48-99ff-12e2a2d7854d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c1bb03-9d37-5f48-99ff-12e2a2d7854d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291773} :answer-field/id #uuid "388ef544-5eeb-55c5-9a22-928e4567de62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1601cf07-a954-57ab-98a1-051fb4994be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1601cf07-a954-57ab-98a1-051fb4994be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291775} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74f45d8-5bc3-53bc-ae02-38dce86cd828" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "270d2cb9-79c0-58ec-983d-1cf82a3c65b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "270d2cb9-79c0-58ec-983d-1cf82a3c65b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291777} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a3ed5d-e8b3-5b70-9759-e7d84e60a072" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e9ef9f0-59b2-578f-bbc7-31473b0fed57" :question/math-academy-id "q-320797" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-6y=9 \\\\ 3y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $9$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-6)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9e4281b-45b9-5850-b450-663e551b37c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9e4281b-45b9-5850-b450-663e551b37c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291780} :answer-field/id #uuid "14a722ce-cd86-500f-834b-94f317a86457" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72328781-dd75-5a77-82a0-8c1ff6390051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72328781-dd75-5a77-82a0-8c1ff6390051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291782} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c995dba-1502-5177-b159-f659f8875718" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa6664cf-c8e0-5040-93e8-aac3939aa28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa6664cf-c8e0-5040-93e8-aac3939aa28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291784} :answer-field/id #uuid "117fb54e-bfa2-503f-9440-27ba8f15512e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1646183f-9371-519e-bbf3-6fa5fa1a7cab" :question/math-academy-id "q-320803" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7y=5 \\\\ 2x+3y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
